WEBVTT

00:09:28.079 --> 00:09:30.329
I know it's going to lead me
to question an assumption.

00:09:30.537 --> 00:09:32.912
And it might be an assumption
I've held for a long time.

00:09:33.537 --> 00:09:36.912
And I'm curious about is this something
you do intentionally

00:09:37.329 --> 00:09:40.704
and how do you get your audiences to
confront that kind of humility?

00:09:41.579 --> 00:09:43.579
Well, thanks for saying so.

00:09:43.579 --> 00:09:48.496
I feel like the the way into a story
for me is usually finding

00:09:48.496 --> 00:09:50.579
a character who is vulnerable,

00:09:50.829 --> 00:09:55.787
who is in a place where they're out of
their depth and they're desperate

00:09:55.787 --> 00:09:59.246
for something. And I think
that desperation is like

00:09:59.246 --> 00:10:06.079
the greatest motivator. And it also it
forces you as a storyteller to know what